Changes in version 2026.8.21 (PR#56)

- SquaredHingeLoss and nn_squared_hinge_loss implemented via cumulative sums in O(n log n) time as a convex surrogate for AUC, from Rust and Hocking (arXiv:2302.11062). Thanks to @tdhock for the guidance and @AmanKashyap0807 for PR.

Changes in version 2026.8.9

- nn_AUCM_loss() and AUCM() gain an imratio argument: the "v1" class prior,
  fixed instead of re-estimated from every batch. NULL (default) keeps the
  batch estimate; "v2" ignores it, having no prior.

Changes in version 2026.8.8

- New batch_sampler_dual(): a fixed positive-negative 
  ratio batch sampler ported from LibAUC's DualSampler.
  In each batch, to guarantee a fixed positive sampler number,
  plain oversampling may be applied on the minority class
  once its pool is exhausted; suitable for losses which require
  the existence of both classes in each batch.

Changes in version 2026.8.4

- nn_CompositionalAUC_loss(): R/torch port of LibAUC's CompositionalAUCLoss.
  Alternates k cross-entropy batches with k AUC-margin batches. Used together
  with optim_pdsca(PDSCA optimizer for the network weights), and
  make_pdsca_callback.
  
Changes in version 2026.8.8

- RandomOverSampler implemented for random over-sampling with optional smoothed bootstrap (ROSE method), ported from Python imbalanced-learn reference. Thanks to @tdhock for the guidance and @AmanKashyap0807 for PR.

Changes in version 2026.8.4
- nn_AUCM_loss() and AUCM() gain a version argument: "v1" (default, LibAUC's
  prior-weighted form) and "v2" (class-conditional form, v1 / (p * (1 - p))).
  "v2" requires both classes in every batch, otherwise the loss is NaN.

Changes in version 2026.8.2

- ADASYN over-sampler implemented for adaptive synthetic sampling, ported from Python imbalanced-learn reference. Thanks to @tdhock for guidance and @AmanKashyap0807 for PR.

Changes in version 2026.7.7
- SMOTENC over-sampler for mixed nominal (categorical) and continuous features ported from Python imbalanced-learn. Continuous features are interpolated as in SMOTE and each categorical feature takes the neighbours' mode as in SMOTEN; neighbours use a distance combining the continuous Euclidean distance with a median-standard-deviation penalty for every mismatching categorical feature. Inherits SMOTE.

Changes in version 2026.7.5
- SMOTEN over-sampler for nominal (categorical) features ported from Python imbalanced-learn. Neighbors are found with the Value Difference Metric (VDM) and new samples are synthesized by per-feature mode (including itself). Inherits SMOTE.

Changes in version 2026.7.4
- SVMSMOTE over-sampler ported from Python imbalanced-learn: trains an SVM (using e1071), based on the minority-class support vectors, discards the noise ones (all neighors are majority) and splits the rest into danger (most but not all neighbors are major, interpolated) and safe (most or all neighbors are minority, extrapolated). Inherit BaseSMOTE.

Changes in version 2026.7.1

- SMOTE over-sampler ported from Python imbalanced-learn. Faithful BaseSampler -> BaseOverSampler -> BaseSMOTE -> SMOTE class hierarchy from imbalanced-learn's design.

Changes in version 2026.6.29

- nn_pairwise_auc_loss and pairwise_auc_surrogates implemented as a surrogate loss for pairwise AUC optimization, from Python libauc reference. Thanks to @tdhock for the guidance and @AmanKashyap0807 for PR.

Changes in version 2025.9.23 (PR#3)

- mlr3_measures$add(...) in register_mlr3().
- change get_nn_ROCAUM_loss fun to torch module class: nn_ROCAUM_loss.

Changes in version 2025.9.8

- batch_sampler_stratified() and batch_sampler_random() adapted from blog.
- measures: MeasureClassifInvAUC, MeasureClassifROCAUM. 
- torch module class generator: get_nn_ROCAUM_loss(env).
